<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harbin</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harbin is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/heilongjiang">Heilongjiang</a> province in north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/songhua-river">Songhua River</a>. It grew from a small settlement after 1898, when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> made it the headquarters of the Chinese Eastern Railway, and became a cosmopolitan city with a large Russian population. Under Japanese rule it was part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchukuo">Manchukuo</a>, and the notorious Unit 731 carried out biological warfare experiments on prisoners at nearby Pingfang.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harbin.jpg" alt="Harbin" width="320" height="167" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: xiquinhosilva · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:26935-Harbin_(29661238117).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
